torch_nn_functional_softplus.improvement_description:
//     OPTIMIZATION: Revert to simple baseline-style kernel with minor improvements
//         - The baseline at 0.005 ms is already very fast; vectorization added overhead due to branching/launches
//         - Use simple grid-stride loop with fast math, single kernel, no tail handling needed
//         - Use 256 threads, cap grid size to reduce launch overhead
//     RATIONALE: For tiny kernels, simpler code with less branching beats vectorization. Avoid the alignment check overhead and dual kernel launches.
